WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.500
<i>Oh dear!</i>

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.630
<i>The results of your sports test
were that bad?</i>

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.630
Yeah.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.960
I was a little shocked myself.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.090
<i>It's almost Golden Week,
so why don't you start exercising?</i>

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.050
E-Exercise...

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.640
<i>Shion was really enthusiastic
about the idea, too.</i>

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>She's really pushing for that!</i>

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.640
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.940
<i>won't you hang out with your friends
during Golden Week?</i>

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:23.940
What?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.570
Um... I-I'm not sure.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.610
<i>You should invite them to do something.</i>

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:31.700
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.030
<i>Your father and I are going to visit you
during Golden Week.</i>

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.370
Really?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.990
Okay, great!

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.040
I'll tell Shion...

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.040
What? You already told her? Whaaat?

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.220
Golden...

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.970
Week!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.230
It's so much fun to have multiple days off!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.230
TEARDROPS ARE FALLING

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.730
Do you have any plans, Hana?

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.480
I'm going to...

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:32.480
jog with Shion every morning.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:34.980
Really?

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.490
Running could be good.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.490
Hana, your lack of strength is...
How can I put it?

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.200
You can't even put it into words.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.750
- Th-That level?
- Yeah.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.710
What are you going to do
during the short break, Kamu?

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.580
A piano recital.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.670
That's about all I have planned.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.840
Huh? Really?

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.550
I wanted to see you play the piano, Kamu.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.050
- Me, too!
- Me, too!

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.560
Then, I'll invite you to the next one.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.060
I'm guessing you have a date
during the break, right, Eiko?

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.560
Why would you guess that?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.150
I just have normal plans with everyone.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.520
See?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.860
13:30 ~ Hina - Rooftop Event
14:30 ~ Momoka Aka
15:30 ~ Midori, Miyuri
16:30 ~ Marie, Yuri

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.860
It looks like a harem route strategy chart.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.740
What is that?

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.700
Where if you make even one mistake,
you get stabbed!

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.120
What? That sounds scary.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.370
Eiko!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.750
A girl from Class 1 wants to talk to you.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.370
Really? Thanks.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.170
Excuse me a minute.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.880
Eiko has already put the moves
on a girl from another class?

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.760
Kamuri, are you studying anything else?

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.270
V-Various things.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.640
Like horseback riding?

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.230
Y-Yeah.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.690
Seriously?

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.520
Whoa! You're like the daughter
of a wealthy family!

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.400
Wh-What else?

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.280
Marimba...

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.150
- Marimba?
- Marimba?

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.570
<i>- Adorable!
- Adorable!</i>

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.740
<i>She hasn't really let her guard down
around me much yet,</i>

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.580
<i>which makes me feel a little sad,</i>

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.500
<i>but Kamuri without Eiko around is cute!</i>

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.590
I'm back.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.300
Welcome back, Eiko!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.050
- Oh, she's back.
- Okay, okay.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.300
You two are really close, huh?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.930
Have you been with each other
since elementary school?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.770
No. We went to different elementary
and middle schools.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.430
- What?
- What?

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.940
During sixth grade,
we played for a few days, right?

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:34.900
Yeah.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.270
And with that alone, she's this attached?

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.530
Someone dashing down the harem route
is different from your average person!

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.780
I still don't know what that is.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.490
By the way, what are you doing
during Golden Week, Tama?

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.330
I'm going to an event, appreciating art,

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.960
buying books and meeting up
with a friend who lives far away!

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.920
That's a packed schedule!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.670
Well, depending on the person,

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.960
it could all be the same thing.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.130
The same thing?

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.300
<i>I see. They're all busy.</i>

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.600
I'm free the last day of the break.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.100
Why don't we all do something
together that day?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.140
I'm free that day, too.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:15.230
I'm free.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.110
Th-That day is good for me, too!

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.070
We go well together, don't we?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.150
We really are soul food!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.030
You mean soul mates.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.200
So, what should we do that day?

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.120
Instead of going somewhere,

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.080
why don't we do a study group?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:33.660
S-Study group? Why?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:37.330
After all, we've got placement tests
right after the break.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.210
But it's the last day!

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:45.220
Don't you want to laugh
and bid Golden Week a fond farewell?

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.430
Right, Hana?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.220
Oh, I would be fine with a study group.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.930
Just seeing all of you
would make me happy.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:55.600
Tama loses.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.350
Where should we study?

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.690
At the library?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.440
If it wouldn't be a nuisance,

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.150
we still haven't been to your place, Hana.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.400
I wanna go!
I wanna go to Hana's apartment!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.490
Remember, you said we could hang out there.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.620
Maybe I could make "tama-les"!

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.620
You said I could leave sweets there.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.670
Of course, if you can't...

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.880
I'll put out the welcome mat!

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.000
Are you sure?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.460
That means you're all welcome!

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.500
Yeah.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.920
I know what "welcome mat" means.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.050
- I'm looking forward to it!
- Yep.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:31.140
By the way, I'm not really
going to make tamales!

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.060
<i>Friends are coming to my room!</i>

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.060
- It was only a pun.
- I know.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:36.940
Friends?

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.900
Yeah. Three of them are coming over.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.020
Well!

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.820
Well, well!
That's something to look forward to!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.070
Y-Yeah!

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:49.820
But I'm going back to my parents' house
for the last day of the break.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.280
Oh, I see.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.700
If I'd known, I would've planned
to go home a different day.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.450
I've got it!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.830
Maybe I should have contractors
renovate the apartment!

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.460
There isn't time for that!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.380
Y-You're right.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.210
Then a big cleaning...

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.970
It'll be fine.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:12.260
You've suddenly gotten busy, huh, Hana?

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.100
Yeah!

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.780
What fine weather!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.450
A beautiful day for a jog, right, Hana?

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:40.540
Hana?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.920
Your mom asked me to get you in shape,

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.170
but I didn't realize how frail you were!

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.420
Frail?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.430
I'll at least make up for it

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:53.760
by training you until you're yoked!

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:56.510
Let's aim for 16-pack abs!

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.730
That's too many! That's gross!

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.600
So five more laps! Let's zoom!

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.860
Let's go!

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.110
W-Wait!

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.490
I just had to get
this limited edition stuffed animal!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.750
Sorry to make you come with.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.500
No, not at all.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.630
It's fun just looking
at your happy face, Hina.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:27.800
Eiko...

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.630
You're supposed to get me
with a snappy comeback there.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.390
Oh, you were kidding?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.390
Knowing you, I thought
maybe you were being serious.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:42.020
By the way, a drink like this
always comes with two straws, right?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:46.150
I thought it was so a couple could
drink it together, but is it...

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.150
It's for that, don't you think?

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:56.280
I don't know if you're acting naturally
or doing it on purpose. I really can't tell!

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:10.840
Breakfast...

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:12.920
and lunch.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.720
Thank you for the food.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.730
Thank you for the meal.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:23.350
There was one left.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.570
I couldn't eat another bite.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.860
<i>Going to an event,</i>

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.990
<i>appreciating art,</i>

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.160
<i>buying books,</i>

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.910
<i>meeting up with a friend
who lives far away!</i>

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.160
These are heavy! I'm tired!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.290
But this is awesome!

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.470
We're here!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.220
Dad! Mom!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.010
Hazuki!

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:07.690
It felt like I was waiting a thousand years
with Hana for you to finally arrive.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.570
We were just here recently.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:15.700
As always, Shion is crazy about her aunt.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.200
She sure is.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.250
Huh? This tea...

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.870
You noticed?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.500
I found the tea leaves you said you liked!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.420
Thank you! This is delicious!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.630
Wow, it hasn't been long,
but have you grown?

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.470
I wanted to make you happy
with this, Hazuki! I'm overjoyed!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.220
No, you haven't.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.970
I'm not going to suddenly grow up.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.100
Well, I have.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.970
I've grown by four kilograms!

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.730
Gaining weight doesn't count as growing.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:48.850
Blame it on your mother.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:52.440
She can't seem to kick the habit
of cooking for three people.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.320
Though by the time you come home,

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:59.030
maybe she'll be the opposite way,
with the habit of cooking only for two.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.410
Then I won't get to eat?

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.490
Don't worry.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.990
Your dad will be the one
who won't get any then.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.330
I do need to lose what I gained.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.710
D-Dad, are you okay with that?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.800
Mom?

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.670
Hana, you seem a little more cheerful now.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.170
I'm relieved.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:21.010
Yeah!

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.930
I wanted to meet your friends.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:31.190
Yeah, I'd like you to meet them, too.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.690
All three are so nice and really funny!

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:37.690
I have so much fun when I'm with them!

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:41.990
And when I think about them
coming over, it makes me so happy!

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:45.240
Shion and I made these.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.580
Oh, they're nice!

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.460
Hana's room is so dreary as it is.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.550
<i>I always feel a little lonely
on the day Mom and Dad go home,</i>

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.260
<i>but today is a little different.</i>

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:02.970
<i>After all, my friends are coming over tomorrow!</i>

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.480
Hana!

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:11.900
T-Tama! Good morning!

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.480
Morning!

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.070
Thank you for inviting me over today!

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:17.610
Th-Thank you for coming!

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:22.030
Hana, it's only been a few days,
but have you slimmed down a little?

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:24.530
Maybe it's the result of jogging every day!

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.120
I'm not suddenly
going to lose weight like that.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.040
You ran this morning, too, didn't you?

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:35.540
You ran, didn't you?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.300
You did run, didn't you?

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:42.550
Hana... Tama...

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.050
Get away from her.

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:46.550
Morning!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:47.680
Good morning.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.520
Kamuri, wh-what did you bring?

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.600
Snacks to leave there.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:57.070
You know how squirrels store up food
for the winter, right? It's the same thing.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.480
She's a little animal.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.320
A little animal?

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:05.070
Will we be able to meet your cousin today?

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:09.040
Shion has been at her parents' house
since yesterday.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.080
Oh, really?

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.910
I wanted to meet her.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.670
I brought something for her.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.670
Would you give it to her
when she gets back?

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:20.920
Sure!

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:22.670
Thank you, Eiko!

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.300
It's sweets, so you two should share it.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.930
As usual, you're devoted
to raising the characters' flags.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.140
Again, what are you talking about?

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.980
I can't wait to see
Hana and her cousin's love nest!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:39.820
Nest?

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:44.280
That's...

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.320
Oh, th-that...

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.950
I thought it was kind of overdoing it,

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.080
but since it was there...

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.830
No, it's cute!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:55.960
It sure is!

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.580
It is!

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.920
C-Come in! There's nothing really
in my apartment though.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.760
We're coming in!

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.590
There really isn't anything in here.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.140
It's very tidy.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.720
Well, she did just move here, right?

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.600
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:18.860
You don't even have a rice cooker?

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:22.940
No. I always eat with Shion
in her apartment.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.490
Then what do you do when you're alone?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.490
Um...

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.490
Study, I guess...

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.950
Study? Of your own will?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.620
Are you like some great woman?

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.080
That is impressive.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.330
N-No, it's not.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:39.960
Studying is about the only thing
I have here to do.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:45.050
Then let's forget about studying for today
and just have a good time!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.430
No, we're going to study.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.930
Are you an honors student?
That's not the Eiko I know!

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:55.140
I'm not an honors student,
which is why I'm barely hanging on.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.560
But one thing before we start studying...

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.100
Eiko...

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:00.690
Right!

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:08.030
Hana, Tama...

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:09.280
Happy...

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:10.370
...birthday!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.740
Me and Hana?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:18.160
Your birthday is this month, right, Tama?

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:21.630
And Hana's was on the day
of the entrance ceremony,

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.130
so we're celebrating both
in between those days!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.130
A birthday party before the study session.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:28.970
We have cake.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.510
Cake?

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:35.350
You're even using an item
to jack up your likability rating!

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.640
Jeez, I love you!

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.270
It dropped.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:41.900
Grrr!

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:46.070
I'll use the same thing
to do a birthday event for you two also!

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:48.190
When? When is it?

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:51.490
My birthday is June 20th.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:53.070
October 30th.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.450
I've got it memorized already!

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:58.370
August 5th and December 15th, right?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.710
You didn't get a single thing right.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.670
Here. Happy birthday.

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:04.040
Happy B.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:06.300
Thank you!

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.760
We didn't give Hana a real present
on her birthday, so...

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:10.930
Our second chance.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:14.930
Th-Thank you, Eiko and Kamuri!

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.180
We're the same age, right, Hana?

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.730
The same age...

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:31.400
Hana?

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:33.910
Oh... Huh?

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:36.660
Huh?

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.160
That's strange.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.910
Sorry, but thank you.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.460
Thank you!

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.670
Hana...

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.130
Hana...

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.090
Hana...

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.470
Thank you, Kamuri.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:58.180
You're so touched to get a present
that you're crying, so let's open it!

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:00.270
Okay!

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.600
It's cute!

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.020
One for each of you, from the two of us.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.860
Thank you!

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:15.910
It's like we have to separate
these two lovers.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.160
I-I feel a little sorry for them.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.040
I've got it!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.960
Why don't we leave both here
in Hana's apartment?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.840
Sure, that's okay with me.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:28.670
But are you sure?

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:31.920
Yes! Can I come to see it once in a while?

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:34.720
Yeah, of course!

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.430
Was that just now what you call a "flag"?

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:39.930
Now you're getting it, Eiko!

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:42.680
Let's have cake.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.310
Yay! This is what I've been waiting for!

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:46.810
MATH ANSWER SHEET
First-year, Class 2
Name: Hana Ichinose

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:55.200
This feels slightly off.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:57.820
S-Sorry. I don't have any plates.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.700
And with Shion out, I can't borrow from her.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.330
It's okay. Wherever you are, cake is cake.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.830
Then let's dig in!

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.840
Thank you!

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.680
Kamu is right!
Even without a plate, cake is cake!

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.720
Maybe this is what they mean
by not judging a book by its cover!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.730
I think it's not quite the same thing.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:27.100
Kamu, give me a bite!

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.360
The whole thing?

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:34.820
Delicious!

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.860
Here, I'll give you one, too.

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.450
That's the equivalent value
of that one strawberry?

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.740
Strawberries are amazing!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:46.080
After we're done eating, it's study time.

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:48.330
Why?

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:52.340
Why won't you just let me be happy?

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:56.170
Because if I did, I'm pretty sure
you'd be unhappy tomorrow.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:02.100
You really are good at studying, Hana!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.060
And you're good at explaining things, too.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.350
N-No, I'm not!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:09.270
Hey, could you tell me
how to do this problem, too?

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:11.400
Let's decide on an order! A lineup!

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:12.690
About this formula...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.190
You beat me to it!

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:15.780
No beating me to the punch!

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:20.070
<i>Now I'm glad I shut myself up
in this empty room and studied so much</i>

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.320
How should we decide?

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:22.530
How about a clothespins on the face showdown?

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:23.280
<i>because there was nothing better to do!</i>

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:23.950
No way.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:25.660
Sorry.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.500
Hana, can I use your bathroom?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:30.460
Yeah, go ahead.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.880
MATH 1

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:40.550
Kamuri, what don't you get?

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.050
You get to go first, Kamu!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.760
So, go ahead! Go on!

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:49.060
Th-The equation for question seven...

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:51.520
Equation?
You don't understand the equation?

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:54.650
Kamuri!

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:57.400
Awww, Kamu, what's the matter?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.530
There's nothing to be scared of!

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:05.540
Come on, Hana! Help me chase her!

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.580
Ouch...

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.590
Cut it out. Don't scare her.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:18.470
Humph! Here with her boyfriend, huh?

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:21.090
C'mon, Hana, let's beat it.

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.430
Are you two young hoodlums?

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.360
POTATO CHIPS

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.370
Teacher Hana,

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:45.490
thank you!

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.700
- Thank you, Teacher!
- Thank you, Teacher!

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:51.460
Oh, no, no, no, I'm no teacher!

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.080
Will you tutor us again?

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.840
If you're okay with my meager help,
I'd be happy to anytime.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.710
Can we come back again
even if it's not to study?

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.010
O-Of course!

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.890
Then, see you tomorrow!

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.930
Yep! See you tomorrow!

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.930
Keep the snacks safe.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.910
It's pretty!

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:43.340
Hana,
Sorry, this is a little late, but happy birthday!
- Mom
Happy Birthday.
- Dad

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:42.470
Mom...

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:52.020
There.

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:54.020
That's a good angle.
